      } catch (_) {
        // Кэш недоступен — ничего не показываем, перейдём к этапу сети.
        cached = const [];
      }

      if (!mounted) return;

      setState(() {
        _cachedItems = cached;
      });


```

I need to complete the network request handling and understand how this fits into the cache-then-network pattern for updating the UI when fresh data arrives. I see the issue now. By wrapping everything in a `Future.microtask`, even the initial empty state gets deferred, which prevents the widget from ever rendering with cached data before the network call completes.

The solution is to split this differently: immediately update the UI with an empty list and loading indicator on the next frame, then fetch cache and network data asynchronously without blocking that first render.

